Linux for the Sophgo SG2002 NanoKVM, as used by IronKVM
=========================================================

This repository holds the source of the Linux kernels that IronKVM runs on
the Sipeed NanoKVM (a LicheeRV Nano B with the Sophgo SG2002, one T-Head
C906 core in use). It is a fork of the stable tree (gregkh/linux) so that
every IronKVM branch starts from an upstream release tag and adds only its
own commits. It exists so that the corresponding source of each kernel
IronKVM ships is public. The work itself happens in ironkvm-dist
(github.com/yuzi-co/ironkvm-dist); this repository takes no issues.


Branches and tags
-----------------

ironkvm/<x.y>
    The mainline kernel of IronKVM's second slot (slot B). It starts at the
    stable release tag the build uses and adds, one commit per patch, the
    patches in the order the build applies them, then the NanoKVM device
    trees, then the kernel configurations and this file.

vendor/<x.y>
    The Sophgo/Sipeed vendor kernel of the first slot (slot A), published
    for its source only. No new work happens there.

v<x.y[.z]>-ironkvm.<n>
    A commit IronKVM builds. <x.y[.z]> is the upstream release tag under it and
    <n> counts the IronKVM releases on that base, from 1. A tag is never
    moved; a change to the tree gets the next <n>.


ironkvm/7.3 at v7.3-ironkvm.2
-----------------------------

On top of v7.3, the commits of ironkvm/7.2 (v7.2.9-ironkvm.1) since
v7.2.9, cherry-picked in order:

 1. 81 patches from George Whewell's nixos-nanokvm
    (github.com/georgewhewell/nixos-nanokvm) at
    b5f830aaea42c464b469f6c8d3de73389f66495b, in the order of
    pkgs/sg2002/linux-mainline/patches.nix: the SG2002 support (clocks,
    eFuse, TRNG, SD/SDIO, DMA, audio, thermal, PWM, Ethernet PHY), the
    HDMI-to-CSI bridge (LT6911UXC), the CSI capture, the VPSS scaler and
    the Coda980 H.264 encoder.
 2. 37 patches from ironkvm-dist (socs/sophgo-sg2002/mainline/patches,
    0902 to 0950): the USB gadget (CD/DVD emulation, wakeup, HID options),
    the WAVE420L H.265 and the JPEG encoders, Coda980 rate control and
    memory, the capture and VPSS changes, the C906 vector fixes. 0942 and
    0943 ("riscv: vector: Fix data pointer constraints in context
    save/restore", "riscv: vector: Fix output operands in context save")
    are dropped: 7.3 has them as 572b25f3a6 and 55b1276ef9.
 3. The device trees, in arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/: nixos-nanokvm's
    LicheeRV Nano B-W fragments and the NanoKVM files, composed by
    sg2002-nanokvm-{alpha,beta,pcie}.dts.
 4. ironkvm/configs/: the kernel configurations IronKVM builds.
 5. This file.
 6. Two device tree commits for 7.3's SoC DT: nanokvm-alpha.dtsi names
    its OLED reset line on the PWR_GPIO node the SoC DT now has (gpio4,
    porte) instead of adding that node itself, and the B-W fragment no
    longer overrides the DMA controller's compatible.
 7. The configurations regenerated for 7.3, and (v7.3-ironkvm.2) with
    the NBD, UDF and SquashFS options ironkvm-dist asks for since
    v7.2.9-ironkvm.1.

Each patch keeps the author, date and message of its commit on
ironkvm/7.2. Where a cherry-pick needed a conflict resolved, the message
ends with a line "[ironkvm/7.3: ...]" that says how: the hwrng Makefile,
dma_alloc_attrs() in kernel/dma/mapping.c and the sophgo DT Makefile.

ironkvm/7.2 at v7.2.9-ironkvm.1 is the same series on v7.2.9, with 0942
and 0943, every patch applied with "patch -p1" as nixpkgs applied the
patch files before this repository existed.


How IronKVM builds it
---------------------

ironkvm-dist's socs/sophgo-sg2002/mainline/flake.nix takes this repository
as a flake input pinned to the tagged commit (github:yuzi-co/linux-sg2002/
<commit>); flake.lock holds its narHash, and kernel.pin beside the flake
names the repository, tag, commit and hash. nixpkgs' buildLinux (the
nixpkgs that nixos-nanokvm pins) builds the tree with no further patches.
The configuration is generated there: the riscv defconfig, nixos-nanokvm's
config.nix and the structured options in flake.nix, completed by
"make olddefconfig".

ironkvm/configs/ holds the result of that, as the built .config files:

    trial.config      the trial kernel (flake outputs default and
                      llvm-opt, the same derivation): Clang 22, kCFI,
                      command line with loglevel=7
    shipping.config   the shipping kernel: the same except for
                      CONFIG_CMDLINE (loglevel=4)

The build fails when the .config it generates differs from these files, so
the published configuration is the one that ships. It sets
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH to the commit time of the base tag (v7.3: 1792365298),
the time the files of the kernel.org tarball carry, so the version banner
and the built-in initramfs are the bytes a build from that tarball gives.

The DTB IronKVM boots is compiled with cpp and dtc from
sg2002-nanokvm-<variant>.dts, with the sophgo DT sources and include/ of
the base tag (v7.3) standing in for those of this branch, as
nixos-nanokvm does. Some patches of the series add to sg2002.dtsi nodes
that the fragments also describe (the Coda980 and the VPSS). "make dtbs"
on this branch builds the same files over the patched sg2002.dtsi; the
result describes the same hardware, with the nodes in another order and
other phandle numbers, and it is not the DTB IronKVM boots.


License
